@* The packs on the Architecture page: the four folders a pack is, and every project in them. *@
<section class="band">
    <span class="kicker">packs · what an agent can do</span>
    <h3>A pack is four folders.</h3>
    <p class="lede">Its tools under <code>tools/</code>, what proves it under <code>evals/</code>, its own screens under <code>web/</code>, its tests under <code>tests/</code>: each a project of its own, so you can take the tools without the rest. <a href="/packs">What each pack does</a>.</p>
    <ul class="rules">
        <li><strong>tools/</strong> <code>louis-agent.pack.files</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.git</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.dotnet</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.shell</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.web</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.docs</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.triage</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.paymo</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.devops</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.calculator</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.where-to-buy</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.shop-prices</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.recipes</code></li>
        <li><strong>evals/</strong> <code>louis-agent.pack.recipes.checks</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.where-to-buy.checks</code>: the rules an eval names to prove a pack's answer, apart from the tools, so only the runner references them.</li>
        <li><strong>web/</strong> <code>louis-agent.pack.files.web</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.git.web</code> · <code>louis-agent.pack.recipes.web</code>: a pack's own screens for the sites that use them, on the framework's web.</li>
        <li><strong>tests/</strong> One test project per pack, and an integration test where a pack leaves its process.</li>
    </ul>
</section>
